    "raw": "First, let's establish the total earnings equation for Nigella. Her total earnings for the month are $8,000, which includes her base salary of $3,000 plus a 2% commission on the total value of the houses she sold. Therefore, the commission earned is $8,000 - $3,000 = $5,000.\n\nLet the cost of House A be \\( x \\). Then, the cost of House B is \\( 3x \\), and the cost of House C is \\( 2x - 110,000 \\).\n\nThe total value of the houses sold is \\( x + 3x + (2x - 110,000) = 6x - 110,000 \\). Since the commission is 2% of the total value, we can set up the equation:\n\\[ 0.02(6x - 110,000) = 5,000 \\]\n\nNow, solve for \\( x \\):\n\\[ 0.02(6x - 110,000) = 5,000 \\]\n\\[ 6x - 110,000 = \\frac{5,000}{0.02} \\]\n\\[ 6x - 110,000 = 250,000 \\]\n\\[ 6x = 360,000 \\]\n\\[ x = 60,000 \\]\n\nSo, the cost of House A is \\( \\boxed{60000} \\).\n\nFINAL: 60000",
